    <item>
      <title>What can I realistically do with local AI on a Mac mini M5 Pro (48GB)?</title>
      <link>https://lobste.rs/s/umsitb/what_can_i_realistically_do_with_local_ai</link>
      <guid>https://lobste.rs/s/umsitb</guid>
      <author> by napolux</author>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 11:07:51 -0600</pubDate>
      <comments>https://lobste.rs/s/umsitb/what_can_i_realistically_do_with_local_ai</comments>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I just got a Mac mini with an M5 Pro (base CPU config) and 48GB of unified memory. I want to run as much AI locally as makes sense, but it's hard to separate what actually works day to day from benchmark hype.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What I'd like to do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coding: autocomplete and agentic workflows with local models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Image generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anything else genuinely useful: transcription, RAG over my notes, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which models and quantizations fit comfortably in 48GB and are actually usable, not just "it runs"?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which runtime and tools: MLX, llama.cpp, Ollama, LM Studio, ComfyUI, something else?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What's your setup, and what did you give up on and go back to cloud APIs for?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Real tokens/sec numbers and "this was a waste of time" stories are especially welcome.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
      <category>mac</category>
      <category>ask</category>
      <category>ai</category>
    </item>
